      "content": "When it comes to groups of individuals hanging out in high-density areas, look for clusters of people who seem to be deliberately avoiding eye contact with law enforcement or other authority figures. Also, be wary of groups that are overly loud, boisterous, or displaying excessive energy, as these traits can be indicative of individuals looking to provoke a reaction. Additionally, consider groups that are predominantly male, as research has shown that these groups are more likely to engage in violent or aggressive behavior. Furthermore, if a group is gathered in a way that blocks pedestrian traffic or appears to be obstructing public spaces, it may be a sign that they are planning to engage in illicit activity.",
